# Normalize all text to LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this, Windows checkouts convert text to CRLF (git's autocrlf default
# on the hosted runners). That breaks the UAT gate two ways against the released
# toolchain:
#   * `beamtalk fmt` normalizes source to LF, so a CRLF checkout makes
#     `beamtalk fmt-check` report every line of an already-formatted fixture as
#     needing reformatting (cli_fmt_check_clean went red on the windows leg).
#   * the `lsp` scenarios feed fixture source to `beamtalk-lsp`; CRLF text is not
#     what the project author committed.
# Forcing LF keeps the fixtures byte-identical to how they're committed, so the
# gate tests the toolchain — not git's line-ending rewriting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit binaries (none tracked today, but guard against accidental mangling).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
